  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge management and advocacy for action against the social and ecological crisis in LAC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Caritas in Latin America and the Caribbean play a crucial role in responding to the socio-environmental challenges facing the region. However, to maximise their impact and promote integral human development, they need to strengthen their capacities for advocacy and knowledge management in order to make evidence-based decisions. This project seeks to empower National Caritas to be agents of change that promote a more just and sustainable future. It therefore focuses on three main processes:

1. Advocacy: to strengthen Caritas&apos; abilities to advocate for public policies that promote sustainable development, social justice and sustainable development that promote sustainable development, multi-stakeholder dialogue at the Summit of the Future, and to strengthen the capacity to reduce vulnerability in human mobility, focusing on promoting strategic alliances to respond effectively to the population. 
2. Knowledge management: to build and disseminate relevant and updated information on crucial issues for the region&apos;s development, such as debt restructuring to reduce social and ecological debt, and the contribution of the region&apos;s Caritas to integral and sustainable human development. 
3. Through these actions, the project will bring about a tangible change in the capacity of National Caritas to influence public policies, promote integral human development and build a more resilient future. The project is expected to provide inputs for the action of national Caritas in improving the living conditions of the most vulnerable communities in the region, promoting social justice, environmental sustainability and the human development.</narrative>
  </description>
